## AutoFactory (LaunchDarkly)

Before pushing a branch or opening a PR, run `/autofactory` on the change set.
(In label-gated mode — `AUTOFACTORY_REQUIRE_LABEL=true` — only PRs labeled
`autofactory` need it; bugfix / chore / unlabeled PRs skip the gate.)
It researches the change and, when flag-worthy, creates a feature flag
(targeting off) with the behavior wired behind it, guarded-release metrics with
instrumentation, flag-on/flag-off tests, and a release manifest under
`.release-flags/` — all left uncommitted in the working tree to review and
commit with the change.

- Re-run `/autofactory` after significant new changes on the branch (the
  pre-push gate only checks that it ran on this branch at all).
- A red verdict is the reviewer agent's opinion, not a pipeline failure —
  surface it to the human rather than silently retrying.
- A no-flag outcome (docs, dependency bumps, config) is a clean pass; nothing
  is created and the push gate is satisfied.
